message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: "Equal amplitudes at different prime-race dilations"
abstract: "Only countably many positive amplitudes repeat at an algebraic ratio of distinct heights. These amplitudes are dense from 0 to 5.85 even at integer ratios. At the named amplitude all 1,891 finite pairs exclude rational denominators below 1089356799264850590264254484675820. The factor-200 census gives 56 positive amplitudes and their gap around 1.9735."
